# Verify UI Before Done

Do **not** tell the user a UI/storefront change is **done**, **fixed**, **live**, or **verified** until you have exercised it in a **real browser** (Cursor browser or equivalent) the way a customer would.

Code review, `curl`, HTML string checks, and passing unit tests **alone** are not enough for user-visible behavior.

## When this applies

Any change that affects what customers **see**, **click**, **filter**, **sort**, **navigate**, or **submit** — including:

- `pricing-tool` Vue SPA (`resources/js/**`)
- Shopify theme (`ovs-shopify-theme/**`) on the live/staging storefront URL
- Collection filters, menus, drawers, dialogs, forms, and pagination

## Required before “it’s good”

1. **Open the actual page** the customer uses (correct URL, tenant, collection, or route — not only `?section_id=` unless full-page is blocked).
2. **Hard refresh** or confirm fresh assets when theme/frontend bundles changed (avoid stale JS/CSS).
3. **Perform the user action** — do not only confirm the element exists in HTML.
4. **Assert customer-visible outcomes** — counts, visible rows/cards, URL/query updates, dialog open/close, navigation target, error/success copy.
5. **If it fails customer expectations, keep working** — do not hand off with “should work” or “try hard refresh.”

## Filters (mandatory checks)

For every new or changed filter (facets, checkboxes, chips, dropdowns):

- [ ] Select **one** value → only matching items remain; **count matches** what the dedicated shelf/collection shows when comparable.
- [ ] The checkbox/chip **stays checked** after tap — no flash refresh, no section reload, no spontaneous uncheck.
- [ ] Clear or deselect → full list returns.
- [ ] **Multiselect** (if supported) → union behaves correctly.
- [ ] **Filter combinations** (when shelf has product + brand or other multigroup filters) → each group alone narrows correctly; **both together** further narrows; both URL params stay set; clearing reverses cleanly.
- [ ] **Pagination** → filtering includes products on later pages (or document/limit if server-side only). Never sign off when filter only affects page 1.
- [ ] **Desktop and mobile** panel if both exist (sync, no duplicate-panel desync).
- [ ] **Mobile drawer**: open → tap filter(s) → close → reopen → selections and layout still correct.
- [ ] Changing **Availability** or native facets does not break custom filters (re-test after).

**Stop condition:** If a filter tap causes Dawn `facets.js` to re-fetch the section, checkboxes reset, or the drawer “feels like a refresh”, the task is **not done** — fix and re-click in the browser before replying.

## Clickables (mandatory checks)

For every new or changed interactive control:

- [ ] Click/tap works (not dead, not blocked by overlay).
- [ ] Correct destination or state change (route, modal, expanded section, download).
- [ ] Disabled/loading states behave sensibly.
- [ ] Destructive actions still confirm when required (`confirm-delete-actions.mdc`).

## Storefront-specific (Shopify theme)

- Test on **operationvstudio.com** (or configured `storefront_base_url`), not only local mirrors.
- After `theme push`, verify in browser — CDN/cache can lag behind section fetches.
- Compare filter results to the **child collection** when the hub mirrors department shelves.

## OVS Tools & Supplies collection filters (manifest + e2e)

When adding or changing any `ovs-*-collection-filters` snippet or JS:

1. Update **`ovs-shopify-theme/docs/storefront-ts-collection-filters.manifest.json`** (toggle cases + `mobileSmoke` per collection).
2. Run **`php artisan shopify:storefront-collection-filters-manifest-verify`** — fails if a new snippet/handle is not registered.
3. Run **`npm run test:e2e:storefront-filters`** against the live storefront (check→uncheck desktop + mobile drawer per manifest, plus **combinationCases** when the shelf has multiple OVS filter groups).
4. Do not hardcode new filter cases only in the Playwright spec — the manifest is the registry.

See **`ovs-shopify-theme/.cursor/rules/storefront-ts-collection-filters.mdc`** for the full checklist.

## Final reply must include

- **URL tested**
- **Actions performed** (e.g. “Checked Brushes filter → 9 products; clicked mobile drawer checkbox → same count”)
- **Pass/fail against customer expectation** — not just “HTTP 200” or “needle found in HTML”

If browser testing is blocked (auth, credentials, service down), say so explicitly and list what remains unverified. Do **not** imply the UI is correct.

